#, no-wrap
msgid "We will look at a single simple observable:\n"
msgstr "Titingnan natin ang isang simpleng observable:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The simplest case: a fixed truncation budget for each slice {#the-simplest-case-a-fixed-truncation-budget-for-each-slice}"
msgstr "Ang pinakasimpleng kaso: isang nakapirming truncation budget para sa bawat slice {#the-simplest-case-a-fixed-truncation-budget-for-each-slice}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The available budget for truncation of Pauli terms can vary at each step of the backpropagation.\n"
"To understand how this works, we first look at the simplest case of a fixed truncation budget as specified by the user.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang magagamit na budget para sa pag-truncate ng mga Pauli term ay maaaring mag-iba sa bawat hakbang ng backpropagation.\n"
"Para maintindihan kung paano ito gumagana, tingnan muna natin ang pinakasimpleng kaso ng nakapirming truncation budget na itinakda ng user.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The most straightforward way to specify the truncation budget is by using the `max_error_per_slice` argument.\n"
"In fact, this is what is being done in the [Reducing depth of circuits with operator backpropagation](/tutorials/operator-back-propagation) tutorial. Setting `max_error_per_slice` to a `float` results in each slice being allotted a budget equaling that value.\n"
"In the example below, we set this value to `0.001` which guarantees an implicit truncation error of at most `0.018`, if all 18 slices were backpropagated.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pinakadiretsong paraan para tukuyin ang truncation budget ay ang paggamit ng argument na `max_error_per_slice`. Sa katunayan, ito ang ginagawa sa tutorial na [Reducing depth of circuits with operator backpropagation](/tutorials/operator-back-propagation). Ang pagtatakda ng `max_error_per_slice` sa isang `float` ay nagreresulta sa bawat slice na binibigyan ng budget na katumbas ng halagang iyon.\n"
"Sa halimbawa sa ibaba, itinakda natin ang halagang ito sa `0.001` na nagagarantiya ng implicit na truncation error na hindi hihigit sa `0.018`, kung na-backpropagate ang lahat ng 18 slice.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<div class=\"alert alert-info\">\n"
"Note that any error budget remaining after backpropagating a slice and truncating terms with small coefficients will always be added to the following slice's error budget.\n"
"</div>\n"
msgstr ""
"<div class=\"alert alert-info\">\n"
"Tandaan na ang anumang error budget na natitira matapos mag-backpropagate ng isang slice at mag-truncate ng mga term na maliit ang coefficient ay palaging idaragdag sa error budget ng susunod na slice.\n"
"</div>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We next use the [OBPMetadata](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-obp/utils-metadata-obp-metadata) instance and the tools provided by the [visualization](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-obp/utils-visualization#module-qiskit_addon_obp.utils.visualization) module to visualize the backpropagation process.\n"
msgstr "Susunod, gagamitin natin ang instance ng [OBPMetadata](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-obp/utils-metadata-obp-metadata) at ang mga tool na ibinibigay ng module na [visualization](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-obp/utils-visualization#module-qiskit_addon_obp.utils.visualization) para i-visualize ang proseso ng backpropagation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The top left plot** shows that we have enough budget to begin truncating observable terms after backpropagating the third slice. Starting from the third slice, we know that we truncate at least one term from each slice we backpropagate because we are incurring some truncation error after each slice.\n"
msgstr "**Ang plot sa itaas-kaliwa** ay nagpapakitang may sapat tayong budget para magsimulang mag-truncate ng mga observable term pagkatapos i-backpropagate ang ikatlong slice. Simula sa ikatlong slice, alam nating may na-truncate tayong kahit isang term mula sa bawat slice na ibinabackpropagate natin dahil may truncation error tayong nagagawa pagkatapos ng bawat slice.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The top right plot** shows that the error budget grows to `.003` for the third slice. We see a sharp drop in remaining budget, which means terms were truncated from the observable. This is consistent with what we inferred from the top left plot.\n"
msgstr "**Ang plot sa itaas-kanan** ay nagpapakitang lumalaki ang error budget hanggang `.003` para sa ikatlong slice. Nakikita natin ang matarik na pagbaba sa natitirang budget, na nangangahulugang may mga term na na-truncate mula sa observable. Ito ay tugma sa nahinuha natin mula sa plot sa itaas-kaliwa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The bottom left plot** shows that as we truncate terms from our observable, our overall accumulated error is growing monotonically. This graph also confirms that no terms were truncated until after the third slice had been backpropagated.\n"
msgstr "**Ang plot sa ibaba-kaliwa** ay nagpapakitang habang nagta-truncate tayo ng mga term mula sa observable, patuloy na tumataas ang kabuuang naipon nating error. Kinukumpirma rin ng graph na ito na walang na-truncate na term hanggang matapos ma-backpropagate ang ikatlong slice.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- **The bottom right plot** shows that the number of commuting Pauli groups in our observable has grown to the specified limit of `10`. This plot also shows how backpropagating one more layer would cause our observable to outgrow the specified bound as you can see from the crossover of the black and red lines.\n"
"<div class=\"alert alert-info\">\n"
"Note that in all of these plots, the x-axis enumerates the backpropagated slices, but since OBP works on the end of the circuit, `slice 1` is the very last slice, `slice 2` is the one before that, and so on.\n"
"</div>\n"
msgstr ""
"- **Ang plot sa ibaba-kanan** ay nagpapakitang ang bilang ng mga commuting Pauli group sa observable natin ay lumaki na hanggang sa tinukoy na limitasyon na `10`. Ipinapakita rin ng plot na ito kung paanong ang pag-backpropagate ng isa pang layer ay magiging dahilan para lumampas ang observable natin sa tinukoy na bound, gaya ng makikita sa pagtatagpo ng itim at pulang linya.\n"
"<div class=\"alert alert-info\">\n"
"Tandaan na sa lahat ng mga plot na ito, ang x-axis ay nag-eenumerate ng mga na-backpropagate na slice, pero dahil ang OBP ay gumagana sa dulo ng circuit, ang `slice 1` ang pinakahuling slice, ang `slice 2` ang nauuna rito, at iba pa.\n"
"</div>\n"

