# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Specify slice budget explicitly {#specify-slice-budget-explicitly}"
msgstr "Tukuyin nang tahasan ang slice budget {#specify-slice-budget-explicitly}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you know how to assign a budget to each slice, such that the backpropagation performance is optimized, you might want to explicitly assign a budget for each slice. For demonstration purposes, we will assign the first three slices zero budget and use a  budget of `.001` per slice for the remaining slices.\n"
msgstr "Kung alam mo kung paano magtakda ng budget sa bawat slice para ma-optimize ang performance ng backpropagation, maaaring gusto mong tahasang magtakda ng budget para sa bawat slice. Para sa layunin ng demonstrasyon, bibigyan natin ang unang tatlong slice ng zero na budget at gagamit tayo ng budget na `.001` kada slice para sa natitirang mga slice.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Removing the budget from the first three layers resulted in no terms being truncated until after the fourth layer, as can be confirmed in three of these plots. What might be somewhat surprising is that although the fourth slice had no leftover budget passed to it, a term was still truncated by using the allocated `.001` budget. This is obvious from the **top left** plot, but can also be observed in the **top right** plot, as the leftover budget curve flattens between slices three and four. Another notable detail is that at least one term was truncated from this point on, the same as in the previous example.\n"
msgstr "Ang pag-alis ng budget sa unang tatlong layer ay nagresulta sa walang na-truncate na term hanggang matapos ang ikaapat na layer, gaya ng makukumpirma sa tatlo sa mga plot na ito. Maaaring medyo nakakagulat na kahit walang natirang budget na ipinasa sa ikaapat na slice, may term pa ring na-truncate gamit ang itinalagang budget na `.001`. Halata ito sa plot sa **itaas-kaliwa**, pero makikita rin sa plot sa **itaas-kanan**, dahil pumapatag ang kurba ng natirang budget sa pagitan ng ikatlo at ikaapat na slice. Isa pang kapansin-pansing detalye ay may na-truncate na kahit isang term mula sa puntong ito, tulad ng sa nakaraang halimbawa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The key takeaway is that although we incurred less truncation error in the second example due to zeroing out some slices' budgets, we were able to backpropagate the same number of slices, and our observable contains the same number of commuting Pauli groups. We can confirm that the bound on our error is smaller in the second example by inspecting the **bottom left** plot.\n"
msgstr "Ang pangunahing aral ay kahit mas kaunting truncation error ang nagawa natin sa ikalawang halimbawa dahil sa pag-zero ng budget ng ilang slice, nagawa pa rin nating i-backpropagate ang parehong bilang ng mga slice, at ang observable natin ay may parehong bilang ng mga commuting Pauli group. Makukumpirma nating mas maliit ang bound sa error natin sa ikalawang halimbawa sa pagsusuri ng plot sa **ibaba-kaliwa**.\n"

