# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Specify the budget cyclically {#specify-the-budget-cyclically}"
msgstr "Tukuyin ang budget nang paikot {#specify-the-budget-cyclically}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you have a circuit with some repeatable pattern, such as a Trotter circuit, you might want to specify a budget for that repeated subset of slices and have that budget used for all of the following repetitions of those slices.\n"
msgstr "Kung may circuit kang may paulit-ulit na pattern, tulad ng Trotter circuit, maaaring gusto mong magtakda ng budget para sa paulit-ulit na subset ng mga slice na iyon at gamitin ang budget na iyon sa lahat ng sumusunod na pag-uulit ng mga slice na iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "More concretely, the example circuit we are using has six slices that are repeated three times, for a total of 18 slices. We will arbitrarily assign zero budget to the single-qubit and `RYY` layers, and `.003` budget to each of the `RXX` layers. We will observe how specifying the budget as a length-6 sequence causes the budget to be applied to all 18 slices cyclically.\n"
msgstr "Mas konkreto, ang halimbawang circuit na ginagamit natin ay may anim na slice na inuulit nang tatlong beses, para sa kabuuang 18 slice. Basta-basta tayong magtatalaga ng zero na budget sa mga single-qubit at `RYY` layer, at `.003` na budget sa bawat isa sa mga `RXX` layer. Makikita natin kung paanong ang pagtukoy ng budget bilang sequence na may haba na 6 ay nagiging dahilan para ma-apply ang budget sa lahat ng 18 slice nang paikot.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<div class=\"alert alert-info\">\n"
"Again, note that the slices are backpropagated in reverse order (that is, starting at the end). Therefore, the first entry in our cyclic budget actually gets used for the last slice, the second entry for the slice before that, and so on.\n"
"</div>\n"
msgstr ""
"<div class=\"alert alert-info\">\n"
"Muli, tandaan na ang mga slice ay bina-backpropagate nang pabaliktad (ibig sabihin, simula sa dulo). Kaya, ang unang entry sa paikot nating budget ay talagang ginagamit para sa huling slice, ang ikalawang entry para sa slice na nauuna rito, at iba pa.\n"
"</div>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As seen in the **top left** and **bottom left** images, no truncation was performed over the first four slices since they were allocated no error budget. Slices five and six had some of their terms truncated as budget became available.\n"
msgstr "Gaya ng makikita sa mga larawan sa **itaas-kaliwa** at **ibaba-kaliwa**, walang truncation na ginawa sa unang apat na slice dahil wala silang itinalagang error budget. Ang mga slice lima at anim ay nagkaroon ng ilang na-truncate na term nang magkaroon ng budget.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As seen in the **top left** image, a relatively large amount of error was incurred after backpropagating slice seven, even though that slice was allocated no budget. This is because only about `.002` of the `.006` total budget allocated to slices five and six was used, so the remaining was forwarded to slice seven and mostly expended, as seen in the **top right** image.\n"
msgstr "Gaya ng makikita sa larawan sa **itaas-kaliwa**, medyo malaking error ang naganap pagkatapos i-backpropagate ang slice pito, kahit na walang budget na itinalaga sa slice na iyon. Ito ay dahil humigit-kumulang `.002` lang sa kabuuang `.006` na budget na itinalaga sa mga slice lima at anim ang nagamit, kaya ang natira ay ipinasa sa slice pito at halos nagastos, gaya ng makikita sa larawan sa **itaas-kanan**.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The **top left** and **top right** images show that the small amount of leftover budget is used up between slices 8-10, and new budget becomes available in slice 11, as expected. The **top left**, **top right**, and **bottom left** images all demonstrate the cyclical behavior of the `max_error_per_slice` argument when its length is less than the number of slices. This cyclical behavior would have continued through all the slices, but the `max_qwc_groups` stopping criteria was reached after backpropagating 13 slices, as seen in the **bottom right** image.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng mga larawan sa **itaas-kaliwa** at **itaas-kanan** na ang maliit na natirang budget ay nauubos sa pagitan ng mga slice 8-10, at may bagong budget na magagamit sa slice 11, gaya ng inaasahan. Ipinapakita ng mga larawan sa **itaas-kaliwa**, **itaas-kanan**, at **ibaba-kaliwa** ang paikot na pag-uugali ng argument na `max_error_per_slice` kapag mas maikli ang haba nito kaysa sa bilang ng mga slice. Magpapatuloy sana ang paikot na pag-uugaling ito sa lahat ng slice, pero naabot ang stopping criteria na `max_qwc_groups` matapos mag-backpropagate ng 13 slice, gaya ng makikita sa larawan sa **ibaba-kanan**.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Also interesting is that the number of Pauli groups actually drops after the second round of budget becomes available at slice 11. This is because there were groups with small coefficients that could not be truncated until there was more budget after backpropagating slice 11, so they accumulated in the observable for several iterations. This case also highlights that `max_qwc_groups` must be _exceeded_ for the algorithm to terminate.\n"
msgstr "Kapansin-pansin din na ang bilang ng mga Pauli group ay talagang bumababa pagkatapos magkaroon ng ikalawang round ng budget sa slice 11. Ito ay dahil may mga group na maliit ang coefficient na hindi ma-truncate hangga't wala pang mas maraming budget pagkatapos i-backpropagate ang slice 11, kaya naipon ang mga ito sa observable sa loob ng ilang iteration. Itinatampok din ng kasong ito na ang `max_qwc_groups` ay dapat _lampasan_ para matapos ang algorithm.\n"

