# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cap the total error {#cap-the-total-error}"
msgstr "Limitahan ang kabuuang error {#cap-the-total-error}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In addition to specifying the per-slice error budget, one can specify the maximum amount of error to incur from truncation. Once that limit is hit, no more truncation will be performed; however, backpropagation will continue until the observable becomes too large and one of the stopping criteria is met.\n"
msgstr "Bukod sa pagtukoy ng error budget kada slice, maaari ring tukuyin ang pinakamataas na dami ng error na maaaring idulot ng truncation. Kapag naabot na ang limitasyong iyon, wala nang gagawing truncation; gayunpaman, magpapatuloy ang backpropagation hanggang sa maging masyadong malaki ang observable at matugunan ang isa sa mga stopping criteria.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We next re-run the above experiment, setting a cap on `max_error_total` such that the error budget is expended after backpropagating slice seven.\n"
msgstr "Susunod, muli nating pinapatakbo ang eksperimento sa itaas, na nagtatakda ng limitasyon sa `max_error_total` para maubos ang error budget pagkatapos i-backpropagate ang slice pito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As expected, our truncation error caps out at `.006` (**bottom left** chart). It is notable that in this run we were not able to backpropagate slice 11. This is because we did not have enough budget to truncate terms and the number of commuting Pauli groups grew past the limit of `20`, as seen in the **bottom right** image.\n"
msgstr "Gaya ng inaasahan, ang truncation error natin ay tumitigil sa `.006` (chart sa **ibaba-kaliwa**). Kapansin-pansin na sa takbong ito ay hindi natin nagawang i-backpropagate ang slice 11. Ito ay dahil wala tayong sapat na budget para mag-truncate ng mga term at lumampas ang bilang ng mga commuting Pauli group sa limitasyong `20`, gaya ng makikita sa larawan sa **ibaba-kanan**.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/truncate-operator-terms/extracted-outputs/69c9069a-9038-4319-8dc6-37a1be973ebf-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/truncate-operator-terms/extracted-outputs/69c9069a-9038-4319-8dc6-37a1be973ebf-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It may be desirable to simply cap the overall budget with `max_error_total` without specifying `max_error_per_slice`.\n"
msgstr "Maaaring gusto lang limitahan ang kabuuang budget gamit ang `max_error_total` nang hindi tinutukoy ang `max_error_per_slice`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The output of the cell above might be slightly surprising because the `per_slice_budget` is set to the `max_error_total`. This indicates that the entire available budget will be consumed **greedily**.\n"
"You can think of it this way: the entire budget is available to each slice (because we loop over the `per_slice_budget`). But any budget that has already been consumed will be deducted from the budget that is available at that given point in the algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaaring medyo nakakagulat ang output ng cell sa itaas dahil ang `per_slice_budget` ay itinakda sa `max_error_total`. Ipinapahiwatig nito na ang buong magagamit na budget ay uubusin nang **greedy**.\n"
"Maaari mo itong isipin ganito: ang buong budget ay magagamit ng bawat slice (dahil nag-loop tayo sa `per_slice_budget`). Pero ang anumang budget na nagamit na ay ibabawas sa budget na magagamit sa puntong iyon ng algorithm.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The **top right** image shows how the entire `.018` error budget is made available to the first slice. No truncation is performed until the third slice, so the leftover budget remains constant. The budget monotonically decreases, as the full budget is made available to each backpropagated slice until it is expended.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng larawan sa **itaas-kanan** kung paanong ang buong `.018` na error budget ay ibinibigay sa unang slice. Walang truncation na ginagawa hanggang sa ikatlong slice, kaya nananatiling pare-pareho ang natirang budget. Patuloy na bumababa ang budget, dahil ang buong budget ay ibinibigay sa bawat na-backpropagate na slice hanggang maubos ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is notable that this experiment yielded two fewer backpropagated slices compared to the first experiment in this notebook, which is almost identical. This demonstrates that for some problems, distributing the budget evenly might be optimal. For other problems, allowing slices to greedily expend the full budget might yield better performance.\n"
msgstr "Kapansin-pansin na ang eksperimentong ito ay nagbunga ng dalawang mas kaunting na-backpropagate na slice kumpara sa unang eksperimento sa notebook na ito, na halos magkapareho. Ipinapakita nito na para sa ilang problema, maaaring pinakamainam ang pantay na pamamahagi ng budget. Para sa ibang problema, ang pagpapahintulot sa mga slice na gastusin nang greedy ang buong budget ay maaaring magbunga ng mas mahusay na performance.\n"

