# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cap the number of backpropagated slices and the total error together {#cap-the-number-of-backpropagated-slices-and-the-total-error-together}"
msgstr "Limitahan ang bilang ng mga na-backpropagate na slice at ang kabuuang error nang magkasama {#cap-the-number-of-backpropagated-slices-and-the-total-error-together}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you don't want to distribute their error budget all the way through the circuit but you don't want to greedily expend it either, you can specify the number of slices you intend to backpropagate (`num_slices`), along with a total error budget (`max_error_total`). This will distribute the error budget uniformly (accordingly to `p_norm`) across the input slices.\n"
msgstr "Kung ayaw mong ipamahagi ang error budget mo sa buong circuit pero ayaw mo ring gastusin ito nang greedy, maaari mong tukuyin ang bilang ng mga slice na balak mong i-backpropagate (`num_slices`), kasama ang kabuuang error budget (`max_error_total`). Ipapamahagi nito nang pantay ang error budget (ayon sa `p_norm`) sa mga input slice.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, we will cap the number of slices we might backpropagate at `12`, and we will keep the same total error budget.\n"
msgstr "Dito, lilimitahan natin ang bilang ng mga slice na maaari nating i-backpropagate sa `12`, at pananatilihin natin ang parehong kabuuang error budget.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we will attempt to backpropagate the 12 slices for which we allocated some budget in the previous step. We do this by just passing in the final 12 slices in our circuit. With `p_norm=1`, each of the 12 slices has an available budget of `0.018 / num_slices = 0.0015`.\n"
msgstr "Ngayon, susubukan nating i-backpropagate ang 12 slice na pinaglaanan natin ng budget sa nakaraang hakbang. Ginagawa natin ito sa pamamagitan ng pagpapasa lang ng huling 12 slice sa ating circuit. Sa `p_norm=1`, ang bawat isa sa 12 slice ay may magagamit na budget na `0.018 / num_slices = 0.0015`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since we passed a subset of our slices (in the code ``slices[-num_slices:]``) to ``backpropagate``, we must combine the slices remaining after backpropagation with the slices that were never sent for backpropagation (in the code  ``slices[:-num_slices]``).\n"
msgstr "Dahil nagpasa tayo ng subset ng ating mga slice (sa code na ``slices[-num_slices:]``) sa ``backpropagate``, kailangan nating pagsamahin ang mga slice na natira pagkatapos ng backpropagation sa mga slice na hindi kailanman ipinadala para sa backpropagation (sa code na ``slices[:-num_slices]``).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Once we have combined all of the remaining slices, we can use [combine_slices](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-utils/slicing#combine_slices) to generate the reduced-depth [QuantumCircuit](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit). Next, we inspect how many slices were backpropagated versus how large our observable became.\n"
msgstr "Kapag naipagsama na natin ang lahat ng natitirang slice, magagamit natin ang [combine_slices](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-utils/slicing#combine_slices) para buuin ang [QuantumCircuit](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) na may nabawasang depth. Susunod, susuriin natin kung ilang slice ang na-backpropagate kumpara sa kung gaano kalaki ang naging observable natin.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The plots show that we did successfully backpropagate all 12 slices while keeping our observable under 10 commuting Pauli groups. We can also see that using `num_slices` along with `max_error_total` results in a distribution of budgets across the slices and unused budget is again forwarded to the next slice. This is most apparent in the **top right** plot, as the budget is both expended and replenished throughout backpropagation.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng mga plot na matagumpay naming na-backpropagate ang lahat ng 12 slice habang pinapanatili ang aming observable sa ilalim ng 10 commuting Pauli group. Makikita rin natin na ang paggamit ng `num_slices` kasama ang `max_error_total` ay nagreresulta sa distribusyon ng mga budget sa mga slice, at ang hindi nagamit na budget ay muling ipinapasa sa susunod na slice. Pinakamalinaw ito sa plot sa **kanang itaas**, dahil ang budget ay parehong nagagamit at napupunan muli sa buong backpropagation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is notable that this method of distributing error produced the best results (more backpropagated slices), compared with the first experiment in this notebook and the example just previous this one. All of these examples allotted `.018` error budget, but backpropagation performed differently depending on how that budget was distributed.\n"
msgstr "Kapansin-pansin na ang paraang ito ng pamamahagi ng error ang nagbigay ng pinakamahusay na resulta (mas maraming na-backpropagate na slice), kumpara sa unang eksperimento sa notebook na ito at sa halimbawang kasunod lang bago nito. Lahat ng mga halimbawang ito ay nagtalaga ng `.018` na error budget, pero iba-iba ang naging performance ng backpropagation depende sa kung paano ipinamahagi ang budget na iyon.\n"

